IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cat-domain`
IMPORT `cat-time`
IMPORT `cat-part1-preliminary`

-- Cat Act 2011 (WA) — PART 5, SUBSIDIARY LEGISLATION (ss 76-84); PART 6,
-- MISCELLANEOUS (ss 85-86); PART 7, TRANSITIONAL PROVISIONS (ss 87-88).
--
-- Source: inputs/cat-act-2011.txt lines 683-784.
--
-- Most of Part 5 confers law-making powers. What can be computed is the
-- limits it puts on them — the fine ceilings in ss 78 and 84 and the
-- territorial limits in ss 79(2) and 80 — and those are encoded; the
-- rest is carried as text (phrasebook 9.4) so a reader finds it.

§ `Part 5 — Subsidiary legislation`

§§ `Division 1 — Regulations`

§§§ `76. General regulations`

-- s 76(1): the Governor may make regulations "prescribing all matters that
-- are required or permitted by this Act to be prescribed, or that are
-- necessary or convenient to be prescribed for giving effect to the purposes
-- of this Act." (2): including "(a) registration tags; (b) fees and charges
-- payable in respect of any matter under this Act." INERT: the Cat
-- Regulations 2012 are made under it.

§§§ `77. Regulations that operate as local laws`

-- s 77(1)-(5): regulations may operate as local laws, must say so, are
-- administered by local governments as local laws, and an offence against
-- a local law includes one against such a regulation. INERT.
-- s 77(6): "If there is any inconsistency between a regulation made under
-- this section and a local law made under this Act, the regulation prevails
-- to the extent of the inconsistency."
DECLARE `Source of a provision` IS ONE OF
    `a regulation under s 77`
    `a local law under the Act`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 77(6)
GIVEN a IS A `Source of a provision`
      b IS A `Source of a provision`
GIVETH A `Source of a provision`
`where` a `and` b `are inconsistent, the one that prevails` MEANS
    IF   a EQUALS `a regulation under s 77` OR b EQUALS `a regulation under s 77`
    THEN `a regulation under s 77`
    ELSE REFUSE "s 77(6) decides only between a regulation under s 77 and a local law"

§§§ `78. Provisions about regulations`

-- s 78: regulations may "(b) provide that contravention of a provision of
-- regulations is an offence, and provide for the offence to be punishable on
-- conviction by the imposition of a fine not exceeding $5 000; (c) make a
-- person who commits an offence of a continuing nature liable to a further
-- fine not exceeding $500 in respect of each day or part of a day during
-- which the offence has continued; (d) provide for the imposition of a
-- minimum fine ...; (e) relate the level of the fine to — (i) the
-- circumstances or extent of the offence; (ii) ... previous offences ...;
-- (f) prescribe the method and the means by which any fines imposed are to
-- be paid and collected, or recovered." (a): adopt any text a local law
-- could adopt.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 78(b), (c)
GIVEN `maximum fine`                 IS A NUMBER
      `further daily fine`           IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a regulation's penalty of` `maximum fine` `and daily` `further daily fine` `is within s 78` IF
        "(b)" ... `maximum fine` AT MOST 5000
    AND "(c)" ... `further daily fine` AT MOST 500

§§ `Division 2 — Local laws`

§§§ `79. Local laws`

-- s 79(1): local laws "prescribing all matters that are required or
-- permitted to be prescribed by a local law, or are necessary or convenient
-- to be so prescribed, for it to perform any of its functions under this
-- Act." (3): a non-exhaustive list (a)-(k).
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 79(3)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 79(3) — matters a local law may be made as to` MEANS
    LIST "(a) the registration of cats"
       , "(b) removing and impounding cats"
       , "(c) keeping, transferring and disposing of cats kept at cat management facilities"
       , "(d) the humane destruction of cats"
       , "(e) cats creating a nuisance"
       , "(f) specifying places where cats are prohibited absolutely"
       , "(g) requiring that in specified areas a portion of the premises on which a cat is kept must be enclosed in a manner capable of confining cats"
       , "(h) limiting the number of cats that may be kept at premises, or premises of a particular type"
       , "(i) the establishment, maintenance, licensing, regulation, construction, use, record keeping and inspection of cat management facilities"
       , "(j) the regulation of approved cat breeders, including record keeping and inspection"
       , "(k) fees and charges payable in respect of any matter under this Act"

-- s 79(2): "A local law made under this Act does not apply outside the
-- local government's district unless it is made to apply outside the
-- district under section 80."
-- s 80(1): "If the Governor's approval has been first obtained, a local
-- government may make a local law under this Act that applies outside its
-- district." (2): "A local government cannot, under subsection (1), make a
-- local law that applies to — (a) a part of the State that is in the
-- district of another local government; or (b) a part of the State to which
-- a local law made by another local government concerning the same subject
-- matter applies under this section." (3): if the approval is revoked, the
-- local law ceases to apply there; (4): notice in the Gazette.
@ref Cat Act 2011 ss 79(2), 80
GIVEN `the place is in the making local government's district`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `made to apply outside the district with the Governor's approval` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the approval has been revoked`                                IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is in another local government's district`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `another local government's local law on the same subject applies there under s 80` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the local law applies at the place:` `the place is in the making local government's district` `,` `made to apply outside the district with the Governor's approval` `,` `the approval has been revoked` `,` `the place is in another local government's district` `,` `another local government's local law on the same subject applies there under s 80` IF
        `the place is in the making local government's district`
    OR  "s 80" ... `validly extended to the place`
    WHERE
        `validly extended to the place` MEANS
                "(1)" ... `made to apply outside the district with the Governor's approval`
            AND NOT "(3)" ... `the approval has been revoked`
            AND NOT "(2)(a)" ... `the place is in another local government's district`
            AND NOT "(2)(b)" ... `another local government's local law on the same subject applies there under s 80`

§§§ `81-83. Inconsistency, adoption of codes, model local laws`

-- s 81: "A local law made under this Act is inoperative to the extent that
-- it is inconsistent with this Act or any other written law." s 82: local
-- laws may adopt model local laws, other local governments' local laws, and
-- Standards Australia codes, wholly or in part, as modified, as at a date or
-- (except a model local law) as amended from time to time. s 83: the
-- Governor may publish and amend model local laws; an amendment does not
-- affect a local law that adopted the earlier text. INERT.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 81
GIVEN `inconsistent with the Act or another written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the local law provision is operative, being inconsistent:` `inconsistent with the Act or another written law` IF
    NOT `inconsistent with the Act or another written law`

§§§ `84. Creating offences and prescribing penalties`

-- s 84(1): a local law may make contravention an offence "punishable on
-- conviction by a penalty not exceeding a fine of $5 000." (2): "If the
-- offence is of a continuing nature, the local law may make the person
-- liable to a further penalty not exceeding a fine of $500 in respect of
-- each day or part of a day during which the offence has continued." (3)
-- minimum penalties; (4) levels related to circumstances or previous
-- offences; (5) how fines are paid and collected.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 84(1), (2)
GIVEN `maximum fine`                 IS A NUMBER
      `further daily fine`           IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a local law's penalty of` `maximum fine` `and daily` `further daily fine` `is within s 84` IF
        "(1)" ... `maximum fine` AT MOST 5000
    AND "(2)" ... `further daily fine` AT MOST 500

-- The greatest fine a local law may set for a continuing offence that has
-- run for n days (or parts of days) after the first.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 84(1), (2)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most a local law may fine for a continuing offence, further days being` n MEANS
    5000 PLUS 500 TIMES n

§ `Part 6 — Miscellaneous`

§§ `85. False or misleading information`

-- s 85: "A person must not give any information that the person knows to be
-- false or misleading in a material particular — (a) to an authorised
-- person exercising a power under this Act, or a person assisting an
-- authorised person to exercise a power under this Act; or (b) in relation
-- to an application under this Act."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 85
GIVEN `knows it to be false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `given to an authorised person exercising a power, or a person assisting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `given in relation to an application under the Act`         IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 85 is contravened by information that the giver:` `knows it to be false or misleading in a material particular` `; given:` `given to an authorised person exercising a power, or a person assisting` `; for an application:` `given in relation to an application under the Act` IF
        `knows it to be false or misleading in a material particular`
    AND (    "(a)" ... `given to an authorised person exercising a power, or a person assisting`
         OR  "(b)" ... `given in relation to an application under the Act`)

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 85 "Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 85 — maximum fine` MEANS 5000

§§ `86. Review of Act`

-- s 86(1): the Minister must review the Act "as soon as practicable after —
-- (a) the fifth anniversary of the commencement of this section; and (b) the
-- expiry of each 5 yearly interval after that anniversary." s 2(c): s 86
-- commenced on 1 November 2013. (3): the report is to be tabled "as soon as
-- is practicable after the report is prepared but not later than 12 months
-- after the end of the period of 5 years".
--
-- The k-th review point (k = 1, 2, ...) is the 5k-th anniversary of
-- commencement; each 5-year period ends the day before it.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 86(1); s 2(c)
GIVEN k IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the s 86 review point` k MEANS
    YMD (2013 PLUS 5 TIMES k) 11 1

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 86(3)
GIVEN k IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to table the report for review point` k MEANS
    `the day after a period of` 12 `months beginning on` (`the s 86 review point` k) MINUS 1

§ `Part 7 — Transitional provisions`

§§ `87. Transitional provision for Local Government Legislation Amendment Act 2019`

-- s 87: a person appointed under the old s 48(1) immediately before the
-- Local Government Legislation Amendment Act 2019 s 92 came into operation
-- (7 November 2020, compilation table) "is taken to be an authorised
-- person appointed under the Local Government Act 1995 section 9.10(2) for
-- the purposes of this Act on the terms and conditions that were applicable
-- to the person's appointment under section 48(1)".
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 87
GIVEN `appointed under the former s 48(1) immediately before 7 November 2020` IS A BOOLEAN
      `otherwise`                                                           IS AN Authorisation
GIVETH AN Authorisation
`the authorisation of a person` `appointed under the former s 48(1) immediately before 7 November 2020` `, otherwise` `otherwise` MEANS
    IF   `appointed under the former s 48(1) immediately before 7 November 2020`
    THEN `appointed under the Local Government Act 1995 s 9.10(2) for the purposes of the Cat Act`
    ELSE `otherwise`

§§ `88. Transitional provision for the Dog Amendment (Stop Puppy Farming) Act 2021`

-- s 88(1): "commencement day means the day on which the Dog Amendment (Stop
-- Puppy Farming) Act 2021 section 59 comes into operation" — not yet
-- proclaimed (inputs/PROVENANCE.md), so it is an input: NOTHING until it is.
-- s 88(2): the Department CEO may set up the centralised registration
-- system early and let local governments record in it, or transfer
-- register information to it. s 88(3): "If a local government records
-- information in the centralised registration system under subsection
-- (2)(a), or information from a register maintained by the local government
-- is transferred to the centralised registration system under subsection
-- (2)(b), before the commencement day the information is taken, for the
-- purposes of this Act, to be information recorded by the local government
-- on a register maintained by the local government."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 88(3)
GIVEN `recorded or transferred on`     IS A DATE
      `commencement day`               IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `information put in the centralised system on` `recorded or transferred on` `is taken to be on the local government's register, commencement day being` `commencement day` IF
    `the law is encoded for` `recorded or transferred on`
    AND CONSIDER `commencement day`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE                                  -- not yet commenced: every such day is "before"
        WHEN JUST c  THEN `recorded or transferred on` LESS THAN c
